To include the `STRU` (structure) and `RMD` (remove directory) commands in the proper locations within the sequence of client requests, we can place the `STRU` command before the `LIST` command, as it is typically used to specify the file structure type before listing files. The `RMD` command, which is used to remove a directory, can be placed after the `PWD` command, assuming you want to remove a directory before listing its contents.

Here’s the modified sequence of client requests with `STRU` and `RMD` added:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
RMD directory_name  # Replace 'directory_name' with the actual directory you want to remove
STRU F  # Assuming you want to set the structure type to file
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
QUIT
```

Make sure to replace `'directory_name'` with the actual name of the directory you intend to remove. The `STRU F` command sets the structure to file, which is a common setting before listing files

